content.text:
Use the `@variant` directive with a breakpoint name in your CSS (`src/docs/functions-and-directives.mdx`, "@variant"):

```css
:root {
  --my-var: 1rem;
  @variant md {
    --my-var: 2rem;
  }
}
```

- Breakpoint variants like `sm`, `md` and `lg` compile to `@media (width >= …)`. `max-md` and the other `max-*` variants compile to `@media (width < …)` (`src/docs/responsive-design.mdx`, breakpoint tables).
- Alternatively, write the media query yourself with `@media (width >= theme(--breakpoint-xl))` (`src/docs/upgrade-guide.mdx`, around line 826).
- Custom breakpoints go in `--breakpoint-*` theme variables (`src/docs/responsive-design.mdx`, "Customizing your theme").

I didn't run the `graphify query` that CLAUDE.md asks for before searching, because Bash was denied. I searched the docs directly with Grep instead. The `:root` example is my own adaptation of the docs' `.my-element` example, so I haven't checked it against the docs.

